Feature importance scores (referred to as importance score in this study) are computed using the standard impurity-based method (mean decrease in impurity) implemented in scikit-learn’s Random Forest Regressor. The importance of feature j, denoted FIj, is calculated as:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$${FI}_{j}=\frac{{\sum }_{t:node t splits on feature j }{w}_{t}.{\Delta i}_{t}}{{\sum }_{t\in all nodes }{w}_{t}.{\Delta i}_{t}}$$\end{document}where wt is the weighted number of samples reaching node t, and Δit is the reduction in node impurity (variance reduction for regression tasks) at node t. The resulting values are normalized across all features so that their sum equals 148,49.
